  "body": "It seems behaviour of localStorage in current stable Chrome is as if it has `OverrideBuiltins`.\n\nThat is to say, the following code is true:\n\n``` js\n// Chrome 45 stable\n// Chromium 47 dev\nlocalStorage.setItem('foo', 'bar');\nlocalStorage.setItem('setItem', new Date());\nlocalStorage.setItem('bar', 'foo'); // Doesn't throw\n\nObject.keys(localStorage); // [ \"bar\", \"foo\", \"setItem\" ]\n\nlocalStorage.getItem('setItem'); // \"Wed Sep 23 2015 ..\"\n```\n\nThe spec currently doesn't require this. It would be good to decide whether or not this should become part of the standard.\n\nIt seems current Firefox actually implements this differently. It is almost the same (in that setItem remains callable) however it does so by choosing not to expose `setItem` as an own property.\n\n``` js\n// Firefox 40\nlocalStorage.setItem('foo', 'bar');\nlocalStorage.setItem('setItem', new Date());\nlocalStorage.setItem('bar', 'foo'); // Doesn't throw\n\nObject.keys(localStorage); // [ \"foo\", \"bar\" ] // Missing \"setItem\"\n\nlocalStorage.getItem('setItem'); // \"Wed Sep 23 2015 ..\"\n```\n\nSee also:\n- https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#OverrideBuiltins\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webstorage.html#storage-2\n- [webidl Note: \"[OverrideBuiltins] if the getter is in a partial interface\"](https://github.com/heycam/webidl/blob/a90316a16f639aaa3531208fc0451a1b79a35a7d/lc2.txt#L161-L167)\n- http://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=14913\n",
